      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This should be a user specific setting, not a world specific setting. Users should have the option to set this from their personal settings. To set this on a world basis would cause problems - YouTube's use of this flag may be unreliable, people might want to watch a video in private that's flagged for whatever reason, and so on. Making it a local safety setting would avoid these issues.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-10-30T10:16:50.837Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "There are some videos on YouTube which are NSFL or very much NSFW.\n\nAs a world owner, I do not want to add a custom YouTube player if I cannot block these videos from being played.\n\n(From experience on other platforms, trolls use these videos all the time.)\n\n\nFortunately YouTube has a method that allows you to check the videos, so you can block those videos from playing.\n\nAll you need to do is check in the YouTube API if \"contentDetails.contentRating.ytRating\" returns \"ytAgeRestricted\" \n\n- https://developers.google.com/youtube/v3/docs/videos\n\nWhat I propose, is that you add an OPTIONAL checkbox, that allows owners to filter out that content.",
